--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party source code is bundled in this repository. The Python
dependencies (httpx, playwright) are installed from PyPI at setup time and
are not redistributed here. `playwright install chromium` downloads a
Chromium build from Microsoft, also at setup time.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Crawled content — read this before publishing anything you collect
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Apache License above covers this crawler's source code. **It says
nothing about what the crawler collects.**

Running it downloads article text, AI-generated summaries and page
screenshots from GIGAZINE into `news/`. That directory is git-ignored and no
article content is contained in this repository. Everything it fetches
remains the property of GIGAZINE and its authors:

- https://gigazine.net/

Republishing, redistributing or broadcasting that material — including the
summaries, which are derived from the articles — may require permission from
the publisher. That is the operator's responsibility, not the crawler's.

The crawler is written to be a polite client: it reads the public RSS feed
rather than scraping listing pages, spaces requests out
(`request_interval_sec`, default 1.5 s), and sends an identifying
User-Agent. **Put a real contact address in `config.toml`'s `user_agent`
before running it**, so the site operator can reach you.

